WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.800
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:11.920
Today we are going to see whether NVIDIA’s&nbsp;
modern AI system they call MineDojo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.400
can learn to play and build&nbsp;
things in Minecraft and more.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:22.400
In an earlier episode, we explored a previous&nbsp;
project that goes by the name GANCraft,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:30.160
which performed world to world translation.&nbsp;
What is that? Well, simple, we give an AI a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:36.560
very rough draft of a virtual world, and out&nbsp;
comes a much more detailed and beautiful one.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:43.840
This almost seems like science fiction. Really,&nbsp;
just dream up something, and it makes it happen.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:50.320
And, it gets better, it created water,&nbsp;
it understands the concept of an island,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:54.160
and it created a beautiful landscape,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.160 --> 00:01:01.840
also, with vegetation. Insanity. It even&nbsp;
seems to have some concept of reflections,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:08.480
although they will need some extra work to get it&nbsp;
perfectly right. It even supported interpolation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:15.520
which means that we can create one landscape and&nbsp;
ask the AI to create a blend between different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:23.360
styles. We just look at the output animations, and&nbsp;
pick the one that we like best. And, with this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:30.480
finally, we also have some artistic control over&nbsp;
the mood of the results. Absolutely amazing.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:37.120
But then they thought, why stop there? For&nbsp;
instance, DeepMind has a long history of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:43.840
using AI systems to master all kinds of&nbsp;
games, from Chess, to Go, to StarCraft 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:51.280
OpenAI has a DOTA2 AI project that is&nbsp;
able to challenge a world champion team,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:58.480
so, NVIDIA thought, why not try their hands&nbsp;
at Minecraft? Minecraft is an open world game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:04.800
one of the most played games in the world,&nbsp;
which is kind of like a virtual sandbox.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:12.880
Here, you can build things, explore, but really,&nbsp;
do whatever you wish. It’s a sandbox after all.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:22.320
So scientists at NVIDIA thought, let’s train an AI&nbsp;
to play this game and see what happens. Okay, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:30.880
how? Well, most AI systems of today require&nbsp;
lots and lots of training data. Wait a minute.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:36.560
There is no shortage of that out there in the&nbsp;
internet, that’s for sure. Let me explain.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:42.480
We can have this little AI sit down and&nbsp;
watch hundreds of thousands of Minecraft&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:51.760
tutorial videos on Youtube, 33 years of footage&nbsp;
in total, my goodness, then, have it read over 7&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:59.520
thousand wiki pages, and then also becomes the&nbsp;
ultimate Reddit lurker. Wow. That makes a ton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:05.600
of sense. Just think about it. It can learn&nbsp;
practical knowledge from the tutorial videos,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:11.520
encyclopedic knowledge from the wiki, and&nbsp;
it can learn what makes the best creations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:19.280
the best that are shared on reddit. That sounds&nbsp;
fantastic…on paper. But, there is so much to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:26.080
and to learn about this game, can an AI&nbsp;
really get an understanding of all this? Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:32.160
hold on to your papers, and let’s see together&nbsp;
what this AI could learn from all this data!

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:38.880
But wait a minute! This is a gamer AI&nbsp;
that uses the controller to move around in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:45.520
a virtual world. But how do we instruct it?&nbsp;
Do we need to speak robot? If not, well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:53.440
it doesn’t even understand English text. What do&nbsp;
we do with that? Well, remember OpenAI’s GPT-3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:58.720
which is a neural network model that&nbsp;
has read almost the entirety of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:05.280
internet. This one has proper English&nbsp;
knowledge, so, we plug that in, and bam,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:12.240
now you can read that wikipedia, and it gets&nbsp;
better, because we can now even give it text&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:18.160
instructions. Now let’s see how well it&nbsp;
fares through 5 of my favorite examples.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:25.920
One, we can ask it to explore an ocean monument.&nbsp;
I love this one because the text description&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:33.360
is sufficiently vague. How could a machine&nbsp;
understand what exploring means? Well, humans do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:40.160
and this learns from humans as there must be&nbsp;
tons of tutorial videos out there on exploration.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:46.320
And, it seems to me that it was able to&nbsp;
learn the concept correctly. Loving it.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:50.720
Two, it can encircle these llamas with a fence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:58.720
That is excellent. It understands what object&nbsp;
it needs to use, where to move, where to look,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:03.680
and that not even a tiny gap&nbsp;
is allowed. Very impressive.

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:11.760
Three, this will be a more dangerous quest.&nbsp;
Now scoop a bucket of lava. Oh my goodness.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:17.120
Be careful there! Do not fall!&nbsp;
We are getting there, and…got it!

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:24.080
Four, we can even ask it to build a nether&nbsp;
portal. It builds the correct portal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:32.080
frame and, did it use the correct materials?&nbsp;
Does it work? Yes and yes! Good job little AI!

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:41.600
And, five. It is final boss time. Literally.&nbsp;
Oh yes. Someone was brave enough to ask the AI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:46.240
to fight an ender dragon, essentially&nbsp;
the final boss of the game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:53.520
and the AI was brave enough to try it.&nbsp;
Well, apparently, this is a limited example&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.520 --> 00:06:00.720
as it does not appear to be charging at the AI,&nbsp;
but, the AI seems to know what we are looking for,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:05.600
and what fighting entails in this&nbsp;
game. Starting this game from scratch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:12.560
and building up everything to defeat such a&nbsp;
dragon takes a long time horizon, and will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:18.880
an excellent benchmark for the next AI one more&nbsp;
paper down the line. I’d love to it perform this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:25.440
start to end. Make sure to subscribe, if such a&nbsp;
paper appears, I’ll be here to show it to you.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:30.720
While we are looking at more examples of&nbsp;
what it could do, I have to note that we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:34.800
barely scratched the surface here.&nbsp;
For instance, it understands text,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:41.840
yes, but if we attach a speech recognition AI&nbsp;
to this agent, we don’t even need to write.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:48.880
It can essentially be a little virtual friend.&nbsp;
How cool is that? What a time to be alive!

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:55.120
Okay, so this is MineDojo, an AI&nbsp;
agent that understands English,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.120 --> 00:07:01.840
and can learn to navigate these virtual worlds&nbsp;
